===Pronunciation===
* {{q|noun}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpəʊstˌdeɪt/|a=UK}}
* {{q|verb}} {{IPA|en|/ˌpəʊstˈdeɪt/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-postdate.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[occur]] after an [[event]] or [[time]]; to [[exist]] later on in time.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=David L. Lieber; Jules Harlow|title=Etz Hayim: Torah and Commentary|page=37|text=Because these prophecies of Isaiah '''postdate''' the fall of Babylon (539 B.C.E), they probably refer to that event.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Meg Roser, Charlotte Chalker and Tim Squirrell|title=Spitting out the blackpill: Evaluating how incels present themselves in their own words on the incel Wiki|url=https://www.isdglobal.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/Spitting-out-the-blackpill_Evaluating-how-incels-present-themselves-in-their-own-worlds-on-the-incel-Wiki.pdf|date=2023-01|page=10|work=w:Institute for Strategic Dialogue|passage=For example, the FAQ page comments that ‘the term “incel” is an abbreviated version and sniglonym of the term “involuntary celibacy,” whose usage reaches back at least to the 18th century.”’ The term ‘sniglonym’ is itself an example of deploying verbose language. The word refers to a term whose date of coinage '''postdates''' the pre-existing concept or object it defines.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[assign]] an [[effective]] [[date]] to a [[document]] or [[action]] [[later]] than the [[actual]] [[date]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''postdate''' a contract, that is, to date it later than the time when it was in fact made}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To affix a date to after the event. <!--i.e. put the true date on it, but later-->

